Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["2. Planar Reissner\[Dash]Nordstr\[ODoubleDot]m", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"31b4db4f-0786-404c-a1b8-13f3d503dca9"],

Cell["\<\
Flat transverse metric r^2(dth^2+dph^2), f(r)=-2 mBH/r+qCharge^2/r^2, exactly \
as in the supplied planar calculation. This is not spherical RN and does not \
add an AdS term. Assume mBH>0 and real qCharge!=0. The positive simple root \
is r=qCharge^2/(2 mBH). Both radial sides are checked; neither is labelled an \
exterior by convention. The coordinates th and ph here are planar \
placeholders. These are geometry calculations, not checks of a particular \
matter system or field equations.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f78abd3e-3f7c-7544-9467-3e75bdda98b9"],

