}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Meaning of regularity", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"dfb0d05d-f7c8-7646-bd75-ea0cc4b0732d"],

Cell["\<\
The horizon report checks limits from both sides, equality of those limits, \
non-degeneracy of the transported raw frame and generalised metric, and \
smoothness of the explicit rational radial expressions by verifying that \
their denominators do not vanish at the horizon. Limits that time out, remain \
unevaluated or have unresolved conditions are Inconclusive. The argument \
concerns the invariant local Courant model and its Born-selected connection. \
It does not assert a global extension, geodesic completeness, or that the \
ordinary Buscher metric remains a valid non-degenerate metric parametrisation \
at the horizon.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a1ab0ee2-8d24-584b-bbb9-199fabc20e4f"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]]
},
